ited to the *particular* note required.' The depth of the cup is also important:—'The shallower and more "cup-like" the cup,' says Mr. Blaikley, 'the greater the strength of the upper partials. Compare the deep and narrow cup of the French horn with weak upper partials, and the wide and shallow cup of the trumpet with strong upper partials.'—(MS. communications.)
